  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "When Is the Right Time to Think About Accessible Appliance Space?",
    "text": "When Is the Right Time to Think About Accessible Appliance Space?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "So, you're wondering when the best time is to start thinking about accessible appliance space in your kitchen? It's a great question, and the answer is usually: sooner rather than later! Typically, this kind of planning happens when you're undergoing a kitchen remodel or when you're replacing old appliances. That's your golden opportunity to build in those clearances and accessible heights from the get-go. However, if there’s a new or existing mobility need in your household or business, then the planning should really happen *before* installation. You want to make sure all those critical elements like clear reach ranges, circulation paths, and the ability to operate appliances comfortably are designed in, not just retrofitted. Trying to adjust things after everything is installed can be a lot more complicated and costly. If you’re at the stage where you're just starting to consider what an accessible kitchen might look like, or if you're facing specific challenges with safe reach and transfer space, that’s definitely a good time to bring in a pro. HH Remodeling LLC can help you plan an efficient and accessible layout right from the start. We’re here to help at 303-505-0866.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
}